WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:02.535
-You look stunning as always.

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:05.271
This is your fifth time
on the show,

00:00:05.271 --> 00:00:07.507
and you missed
the whole Zoom period.

00:00:07.507 --> 00:00:10.877
So we've only had you in person,
and I'm so grateful for that.

00:00:10.877 --> 00:00:13.780
-Lucky me.
-Lucky us.

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:16.349
So, this is so --
this must be so exciting.

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:18.818
And I want to talk about
your history with Aretha,

00:00:18.818 --> 00:00:20.953
because you have some,
which is really cool,

00:00:20.953 --> 00:00:23.589
including she came to see you
in "The Color Purple."

00:00:23.589 --> 00:00:25.357
-She did.
-You knew.

00:00:25.357 --> 00:00:28.294
Your co-stars,
Cynthia Erivo, Danielle Brooks,

00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:31.030
and others, they didn't know,
and you chose not to tell them.

00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:34.233
You had the power to give
this information to them.

00:00:34.233 --> 00:00:35.735
Was it just that
you didn't want them

00:00:35.735 --> 00:00:37.069
to be in their head
during the show?

00:00:37.069 --> 00:00:39.739
-Well, yeah, because a lot
of times when you're doing

00:00:39.739 --> 00:00:41.807
a live show,
you kind of don't want to know

00:00:41.807 --> 00:00:42.809
who's in the audience.
-Sure.

00:00:42.809 --> 00:00:44.710
-And who gonna be able
to perform

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:46.212
and Aretha Franklin
is in the audience?

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:49.082
I was like,
"I'm not going to tell them.

00:00:49.082 --> 00:00:51.184
I'm gonna wait,"
and then I'm glad I did

00:00:51.184 --> 00:00:52.518
because all of them were like,

00:00:52.518 --> 00:00:54.888
"I'm so glad you didn't tell us
that she was here."

00:00:54.888 --> 00:00:56.656
I was the only one that knew.
Yeah.

00:00:56.656 --> 00:00:58.057
-It's a lot -- You're right.

00:00:58.057 --> 00:01:00.927
It's a lot to know,
because as an actor,

00:01:00.927 --> 00:01:02.861
you know, you want to
embody your character.

00:01:02.861 --> 00:01:04.730
But if that character knows
Aretha is in the house,

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:05.799
they're gonna be different too.

00:01:05.799 --> 00:01:07.967
-Nobody would be able
to do nothing.

00:01:07.967 --> 00:01:10.603
So I was like, "I don't want to
crash the show tonight.

00:01:10.603 --> 00:01:12.771
I'm not going to tell them."
-And is she the kind of person

00:01:12.771 --> 00:01:14.640
when she comes to the show,
that everyone --

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:16.376
she sticks around after?
Did people get a chance

00:01:16.376 --> 00:01:17.544
to say hello?
-She did.

00:01:17.544 --> 00:01:20.280
I got to introduce her
to the entire cast.

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:21.814
Danielle got to meet her,
Cynthia got --

00:01:21.814 --> 00:01:25.518
the entire cast got to meet her,
and she was so gracious

00:01:25.518 --> 00:01:28.955
to just, you know,
take photos with everyone.

00:01:28.955 --> 00:01:31.957
Everybody was like, I mean,
people who I didn't even know

00:01:31.957 --> 00:01:34.393
was in the house
came down to meet Aretha.

00:01:34.393 --> 00:01:37.063
-Yeah. We were lucky enough
to have her here once,

00:01:37.063 --> 00:01:40.165
and I feel as though
you can't --

00:01:40.165 --> 00:01:42.201
you know, I had a little bit of
time with her.

00:01:42.201 --> 00:01:44.070
And I feel like I didn't
get enough out of it

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:46.839
because at the same time,
it's like talking to someone --

00:01:46.839 --> 00:01:50.476
she feels like, not -- you know,
I don't mean to say that --

00:01:50.476 --> 00:01:52.445
she was, like, special
in a way that you forgot

00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:54.414
that she could answer questions
and talk.

00:01:54.414 --> 00:01:56.015
I just thought I would
just look at her.

00:01:56.015 --> 00:01:57.083
And then I realized I was
making a fool out of myself.

00:01:57.083 --> 00:01:58.317
-I kind of felt the same way.
-Yeah.

00:01:58.317 --> 00:02:00.219
-Like, okay, this is --

00:02:00.219 --> 00:02:03.356
like, how do you engage with
the Queen of Soul?

00:02:03.356 --> 00:02:04.891
-Exactly.
-What do you say?

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:07.059
-Well, so, you had
a unique situation,

00:02:07.059 --> 00:02:09.161
which is she hand-picked you --
-She did.

00:02:09.161 --> 00:02:11.698
-So you at least --
I don't know.

00:02:11.698 --> 00:02:13.466
When you got to be with her,

00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:15.901
you were allowed to ask
questions, right?

00:02:15.901 --> 00:02:17.370
-Y-Yeah.

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:19.105
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.105 --> 00:02:20.506
Yes, I guess.

00:02:20.506 --> 00:02:21.907
I mean, but when Aretha spoke,

00:02:21.907 --> 00:02:23.742
you just sat and you listen,
you know?

00:02:23.742 --> 00:02:26.579
But just -- I'm still in awe
of her picking me.

00:02:26.579 --> 00:02:30.516
What I wish I had asked is,
"Okay, why?"

00:02:30.516 --> 00:02:33.552
You know, what would I say to
Miss Aretha Franklin?

00:02:33.552 --> 00:02:35.588
What would you say?
I don't know.

00:02:35.588 --> 00:02:39.291
-How did you find out that she
had thought you would be

00:02:39.291 --> 00:02:41.494
the right person
to take this role on?

00:02:41.494 --> 00:02:43.563
-Well, we first met
15 years ago.

00:02:43.563 --> 00:02:45.397
This was right after I won
the Oscar for "Dreamgirls."

00:02:45.397 --> 00:02:48.601
We met here in New York.

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:50.936
And she was like,
"What, you're shy or something?"

00:02:50.936 --> 00:02:52.171
I was like, "Well, I am sitting

00:02:52.171 --> 00:02:54.106
at the table
with Aretha Franklin.

00:02:54.106 --> 00:02:55.575
Jesus!"

00:02:55.575 --> 00:02:58.444
And then it wasn't until "Color
Purple" when she called me.

00:02:58.444 --> 00:03:00.346
She said,
"Now, I've made my decision,

00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:02.214
and it is you
who I want to play me.

00:03:02.214 --> 00:03:04.484
Don't go and tell the pr--
Don't say a thing."

00:03:04.484 --> 00:03:05.985
And I said, "Yes, ma'am,
I won't."

00:03:05.985 --> 00:03:07.687
And then the next day
she went and told it.

00:03:07.687 --> 00:03:09.088
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.088 --> 00:03:12.157
-Now, did you know that based on
the first time you met her?

00:03:12.157 --> 00:03:14.327
Did you know this was something
she was thinking about?

00:03:14.327 --> 00:03:16.462
When you first met her
15 years ago?

00:03:16.462 --> 00:03:18.030
-Yeah. That's what
that meeting was for.

00:03:18.030 --> 00:03:20.699
But it was just talks of it, and
there was no script at the time.

00:03:20.699 --> 00:03:24.537
And then years later then,
she came back again,

00:03:24.537 --> 00:03:26.572
but it was always in the back
of my mind from that moment,

00:03:26.572 --> 00:03:29.108
so anytime -- Because I was
able to do a lot of tributes

00:03:29.108 --> 00:03:31.210
to her throughout my career.
-Sure.

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:34.781
-So after a while, in my mind,
I'm like, "This is my audition."

00:03:34.781 --> 00:03:36.316
You know?
I always had that in my mind.

00:03:36.316 --> 00:03:37.850
-And speaking of auditions,

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:40.687
you did an Aretha song when you
auditioned for "American Idol."

00:03:40.687 --> 00:03:42.254
So this was not something --

00:03:42.254 --> 00:03:44.990
You just didn't start angling
for this late in life.

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:47.392
You had always been
sort of leaning on Aretha.

00:03:47.392 --> 00:03:49.962
-Yeah. I mean, she's always
been present in my life

00:03:49.962 --> 00:03:51.931
unconsciously in some way.

00:03:51.931 --> 00:03:54.634
Like, even growing up in church,
I didn't realize all the songs,

00:03:54.634 --> 00:03:56.269
the gospel songs
I grew up singing

00:03:56.269 --> 00:03:58.438
came from her "Amazing Grace"
album.

00:03:58.438 --> 00:04:00.807
And that was my introduction
to the world,

00:04:00.807 --> 00:04:03.809
me on "American Idol" saying,
"Hi, my name is Jennifer Hudson,

00:04:03.809 --> 00:04:05.311
and I'm going to sing
Aretha Franklin,

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:06.679
'Share Your Love with Me.'"

00:04:06.679 --> 00:04:08.147
And now here I am.

00:04:08.147 --> 00:04:11.484
-And did you --
So, did you open for her ever?

00:04:11.484 --> 00:04:14.086
-I did.
-But you didn't meet her then.

00:04:14.086 --> 00:04:14.920
-Yes.
-Okay.

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:16.022
-Okay, hold on.

00:04:16.022 --> 00:04:18.891
So that was before
we had our meeting.

00:04:18.891 --> 00:04:21.694
This was right after I was
eliminated from "American Idol,"

00:04:21.694 --> 00:04:23.062
seventh place, thank you.
-Yeah.

00:04:23.062 --> 00:04:24.997
And it should be noted,

00:04:24.997 --> 00:04:27.066
all the other six
are bigger stars than you.

00:04:27.066 --> 00:04:28.901
So...
[ Laughter ]

00:04:28.901 --> 00:04:30.737
-They're stars
in their own right.

00:04:30.737 --> 00:04:32.671
[ Laughter ]

00:04:32.671 --> 00:04:34.740
So, I got to open up for her.

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:36.708
She only allowed comedians
to open up for her.

00:04:36.708 --> 00:04:37.977
-I didn't realize that.
-Yeah.

00:04:37.977 --> 00:04:39.445
-So she didn't like to have
a singer before her?

00:04:39.445 --> 00:04:42.114
-No. That's what I was told.

00:04:42.114 --> 00:04:43.750
But she said that I could
open up for her show.

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:45.785
So I got to open up for her,

00:04:45.785 --> 00:04:48.587
watch her sing,
and give her flowers.

00:04:48.587 --> 00:04:50.023
-That's pretty good.

00:04:50.023 --> 00:04:53.793
Now, when you put together --
do you think about the fact that

00:04:53.793 --> 00:04:55.695
everyone who is going to
see you open

00:04:55.695 --> 00:04:58.297
is going to see Aretha
after you,

00:04:58.297 --> 00:05:00.566
does that affect how you put
together your run list

00:05:00.566 --> 00:05:03.368
of the songs you're going to do,
your set list?

00:05:03.368 --> 00:05:05.237
-It should.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:05.237 --> 00:05:06.638
I think.

00:05:06.638 --> 00:05:09.142
I remember her saying,
"Don't sing none of my songs."

00:05:09.142 --> 00:05:10.342
[ Laughter ]

00:05:10.342 --> 00:05:13.979
I was like, "Yes, ma'am."

00:05:13.979 --> 00:05:16.182
But what did I even sing?

00:05:16.182 --> 00:05:18.451
I think I sang
my own original material?

00:05:18.451 --> 00:05:20.219
-That's good.
-But I didn't sing her song,

00:05:20.219 --> 00:05:22.188
I'll tell you that.
-You know what?

00:05:22.188 --> 00:05:23.456
I like two things about that.

00:05:23.456 --> 00:05:25.558
One, first of all, I think
you would have assumed

00:05:25.558 --> 00:05:26.892
not to sing any of her songs.
-Right.

00:05:26.892 --> 00:05:29.195
-But do I like that Aretha knew,
"You know what?

00:05:29.195 --> 00:05:30.830
Better safe than sorry.

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:33.699
I'm going to lay it out
exactly how I want it to be."

00:05:33.699 --> 00:05:35.234
-She let me know.

00:05:35.234 --> 00:05:37.870
-You had a pretty cool --
You did a premiere for this,

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:40.640
or I should say a party of sorts
out on Martha's Vineyard,

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:42.742
where you showed the film.
-Yes.

00:05:42.742 --> 00:05:44.576
-And do you think
it was the kind of party --

00:05:44.576 --> 00:05:46.345
Do you think if Aretha
could still be with us,

00:05:46.345 --> 00:05:48.047
she would have enjoyed it?
-I think so.

00:05:48.047 --> 00:05:50.650
They had good food.
She loved to eat.

00:05:50.650 --> 00:05:54.420
And good music,
which was her music.

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:56.155
So I know she would've
loved that.

00:05:56.155 --> 00:05:57.924
And it was a celebration of her.
So I think so.

00:05:57.924 --> 00:05:59.558
-Was it the kind of food that
she would have liked to eat?

00:05:59.558 --> 00:06:01.026
Did thought go into
putting together

00:06:01.026 --> 00:06:02.261
an Aretha-friendly menu?

00:06:02.261 --> 00:06:03.729
-I don't know if it was
an Aretha menu though.

00:06:03.729 --> 00:06:05.297
-Okay, gotcha.
-Yeah.

00:06:05.297 --> 00:06:07.900
She would've liked some greens.

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:09.501
-Yeah, she would've liked
some greens.

00:06:09.501 --> 00:06:11.938
There was another --

00:06:11.938 --> 00:06:13.171
I don't know if you've been
reading the news.

00:06:13.171 --> 00:06:15.674
There was another party
on Martha's Vineyard.

00:06:15.674 --> 00:06:17.410
-It was. Were you there?

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:19.178
-No.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:19.178 --> 00:06:22.515
But only -- I had a conflict,
which was I wasn't invited.

00:06:22.515 --> 00:06:23.882
[ Laughter ]

00:06:23.882 --> 00:06:25.384
What about you?
Were you invited?

00:06:25.384 --> 00:06:26.918
-You know what?

00:06:26.918 --> 00:06:28.487
I don't know if I was.

00:06:28.487 --> 00:06:30.756
But I did sing for
Obama's 50th birthday.

00:06:30.756 --> 00:06:32.291
-Really?
-I sure did.

00:06:32.291 --> 00:06:33.559
-Well, I mean, I feel like

00:06:33.559 --> 00:06:36.462
you got to get the invite
to the 60th.

00:06:36.462 --> 00:06:38.264
Did you do one of his songs?

00:06:38.264 --> 00:06:41.000
[ Laughter ]

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:45.070
-You know, I sang him
"Happy Birthday" for that.

00:06:45.070 --> 00:06:46.638
I didn't really sing much else.

00:06:46.638 --> 00:06:50.642
But that was I guess 10 years
ago, and they did see the film.

00:06:50.642 --> 00:06:51.877
-They did see the film?
-They did.

00:06:51.877 --> 00:06:52.945
-How do you know they saw it?

00:06:52.945 --> 00:06:54.313
-Because they called me
afterwards,

00:06:54.313 --> 00:06:55.982
him and Michelle.

00:06:55.982 --> 00:06:58.384
-Like, it wasn't like --
This was them on the phone?

00:06:58.384 --> 00:06:59.484
-This was them on the phone.
-Gotcha.

00:06:59.484 --> 00:07:01.186
-FaceTime, too.
-Oh, FaceTime?

00:07:01.186 --> 00:07:04.724
-Take that!
[ Laughter ]

00:07:04.724 --> 00:07:05.924
-Well, that's good 'cause, like,

00:07:05.924 --> 00:07:07.727
a lot of people do impressions
of them.

00:07:07.727 --> 00:07:09.628
But if it was FaceTime,
it was definitely them.

00:07:09.628 --> 00:07:11.497
-It was them.
-That's really cool.

00:07:11.497 --> 00:07:13.499
And also really cool,
we were talking backstage,

00:07:13.499 --> 00:07:15.534
you're going to do a concert
at the Apollo?

00:07:15.534 --> 00:07:17.602
-I am.
-And this is kind of --

00:07:17.602 --> 00:07:19.772
We're in this time now
where people are getting back

00:07:19.772 --> 00:07:21.340
in front of people again
to do their show.

00:07:21.340 --> 00:07:22.808
You must be so excited.

00:07:22.808 --> 00:07:25.445
-I'm so excited to just look
somebody upside the head

00:07:25.445 --> 00:07:27.747
and sing to them
and be in the presence.

00:07:27.747 --> 00:07:30.482
So thank you, Mastercard,
for this amazing moment.

00:07:30.482 --> 00:07:33.119
And it's gonna be a good time.
I can't wait to sing.

00:07:33.119 --> 00:07:34.487
I'm gonna sing
some Aretha songs.

00:07:34.487 --> 00:07:35.654
-You're going to do some Aretha?

00:07:35.654 --> 00:07:37.323
-If you want, you can come
and sing with me.

00:07:37.323 --> 00:07:39.225
-I would love that.
Thank you so much.

00:07:39.225 --> 00:07:41.427
I feel like no one ever asks.

00:07:41.427 --> 00:07:45.297
I'll do the vowels in "Respect."

00:07:45.297 --> 00:07:47.300
You can do --
-Can we practice?

00:07:47.300 --> 00:07:49.768
-I would love it.
Let's practice later.

00:07:49.768 --> 00:07:51.570
Hey, thank you so much
for being here.

00:07:51.570 --> 00:07:53.906
It's just a delight to see you.
"Respect" is in theaters now.

